// Title: SysKey Registry Keys Access
// Sigma ID: 9a4ff3b8-6187-4fd2-8e8b-e0eae1129495
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Roberto Rodriguez @Cyb3rWard0g
// Date: 2019-08-12 | Modified: 2021-11-27
// ATT&CK: discovery, T1012
// Description: Detects handle requests and access operations to specific registry keys to calculate the SysKey
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://threathunterplaybook.com/hunts/windows/190625-RegKeyAccessSyskey/notebook.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/builtin/security/win_security_syskey_registry_access.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey endswith "lsa\\JD" or RegistryKey endswith "lsa\\GBG" or RegistryKey endswith "lsa\\Skew1" or RegistryKey endswith "lsa\\Data"
